CHAPTER VII — VR COMBAT SYSTEMS
VR in Obsidian Protocol is optional, seamless, and fully synchronized with the autonomous RTS simulation.
Players can jump into drones, pilot air units, perform recon sweeps, designate strikes, or fight full dogfights — all while the RTS battle continues autonomously.

This chapter defines every VR system, control layer, combat mechanic, and integration rule.

7.1 VR Dogfight Rules
VR dogfights allow players to pilot air units in full cockpit simulation while the RTS battle continues.

Supported Units
Any air unit with:

Cockpit

Sensor suite

Maneuvering capability

Weapons

Examples: Warden, Beacon, Iris, Nightguard, Overseer, Vector, Watchtower.

Dogfight Engagement Loop
Acquire target

Manage altitude band

Maintain energy

Avoid missile lock

Engage with guns/missiles

Break off or pursue

Altitude Bands
Altitude determines:

Visibility

Sensor strength

Missile lock reliability

Maneuverability

Vulnerability to AA

Bands:

Low — strafing, high risk

Mid — balanced

High — air superiority

Extreme — recon, stealth, long‑range missiles

Energy Management
Energy determines:

Speed

Turn rate

Afterburner duration

Climb ability

Players must balance:

Throttle

Afterburner

Maneuvering

Weapon firing

Missile Lock & Countermeasures
Missile lock requires:

Sensor alignment

Stable flight

Target within cone

No occlusion

Countermeasures:

Flares

Chaff

ECM bursts

High‑G break turns

Damage Feedback
Damage is communicated through:

